From: Korri downstream <maintainers@korri.invalid>
Date: Thu, 4 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] WaylandBackend: allow disabling explicit sync via env

On render-only Vulkan ICDs without working drm_syncobj timeline-semaphore
signalling (PanVK on Mali-G52 / Rockchip RK3566), the explicit-sync acquire
timeline point gamescope attaches to each buffer it commits to the host
compositor (Sway/wlroots) never signals. The host then waits forever on the
acquire point before compositing, so it never sends the next frame callback /
presentation feedback. gamescope keeps holding the nested client's buffer,
the client (e.g. RetroArch) blocks in eglSwapBuffers, and the whole nested
present loop deadlocks after the first couple of frames.

Add a GAMESCOPE_DISABLE_EXPLICIT_SYNC env switch that forces the Wayland
backend to report no explicit-sync support, falling back to implicit dmabuf
fences (which Panfrost/PanVK do set on the GEM buffer). On Adreno (SM8550)
and Steam-Deck-class hardware the env is unset and behaviour is unchanged.
---
 src/Backends/WaylandBackend.cpp | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

--- a/src/Backends/WaylandBackend.cpp
+++ b/src/Backends/WaylandBackend.cpp
@@ -2295,6 +2295,14 @@
 
     bool CWaylandBackend::SupportsExplicitSync() const
     {
+        // On render-only Vulkan ICDs without working drm_syncobj timeline
+        // signalling (e.g. PanVK on Mali-G52 / RK3566), the explicit-sync
+        // acquire timeline point we attach to buffers committed to the host
+        // compositor never signals, so the host waits forever on the acquire
+        // and the nested present loop deadlocks after a few frames. Allow
+        // forcing implicit dmabuf-fence sync via env in that case.
+        if ( getenv( "GAMESCOPE_DISABLE_EXPLICIT_SYNC" ) )
+            return false;
         return true;
     }
 
